WEBVTT


00:00:00.540 --> 00:00:02.240
And let me just say this,

00:00:02.300 --> 00:00:07.100
the trust is a vehicle which takes assets and property from one place to another.

00:00:07.101 --> 00:00:09.600
It's also the instrument that's gonna set you free.

00:00:10.180 --> 00:00:13.360
When you have a trust is not just some pages in a folder,

00:00:13.820 --> 00:00:16.280
nor should it be recorded on the public record.

00:00:16.940 --> 00:00:19.720
I don't know where that came from. Anywho,

00:00:20.300 --> 00:00:23.140
the trust serves one purpose and one purpose only,

00:00:23.141 --> 00:00:26.920
which is to hold property that's protected by a bank.

00:00:27.380 --> 00:00:28.860
Y'all gotta look at it like this.

00:00:28.861 --> 00:00:31.360
Our states is held in a public trust,

00:00:31.940 --> 00:00:34.540
so it's protected by the bank,

00:00:34.541 --> 00:00:38.740
even from us. But when you have a private trust that you go take to them

00:00:38.741 --> 00:00:43.300
and you give them that, they will move the assets for you into that private trust

00:00:43.301 --> 00:00:45.160
because that's what you told them to do.

00:00:46.060 --> 00:00:48.880
Moving in trust has to be understood,

00:00:49.140 --> 00:00:51.460
not only just saying you have a trust,

00:00:51.461 --> 00:00:53.180
if you don't know what to do with the trust,

00:00:53.181 --> 00:00:54.840
you not really moving in trust.
